window.DS3_CHUNK("armor",[{"id":"alva-set","kind":"armor","name":"Alva Set","page":"Alva Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Alva_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":24.612,"strike":20.492,"slash":24.612,"thrust":22.699,"mag":19.2,"fire":22.699,"ltn":19.2,"dark":21.771},"res":{"bld":145,"psn":88,"fst":93,"cur":55},"weight":22,"poise":22.03,"weight_class":"","desc":"Protection of Alva, seeker of the spurned. This steel body armor was trimmed to reduce weight.\nTo this day, troubadours sing of tales of the wandering knight Alva and his travels, and of his involvement with the saint and the witch. Needless to say, the songs traditionally end in tragedy.","avail":"<p>The entire set is found on a corpse near <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a>'s cell in <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, on the lowest level guarded by numerous Jailers. The set will only appear once Alva, Seeker of the Spurned has been defeated in the area between the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Distant Manor<\/a> and <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a> bonfires.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Alva_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"antiquated-plain-set","kind":"armor","name":"Antiquated Plain Set","page":"Antiquated Plain Set","img":"assets/img/Antiquated_Plain_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":6.669,"strike":5.609,"slash":4.931,"thrust":4.443,"mag":21.839,"fire":19.13,"ltn":20.888,"dark":21.145},"res":{"bld":59,"psn":93,"fst":50,"cur":118},"weight":6,"poise":1.59,"weight_class":"","desc":"Ordinary garb from an ancient land of sorcery. The gold embellishments betray a faint residue of magic, but this clothing was never intended for battle.\nWhen a mission visited the Ringed City long ago, one of its younger missionaries elected to stay behind. It was he who became the last recorded Spear of the Church.","avail":"<ul><li>The Loincloth is found in <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>, within <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">Earthen Peak's<\/a> swamp guarded by Poisonhorn Bugs and an Angel.<\/li><li>The garb and gloves are found within <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">the Ringed City<\/a>, on a corpse in front of the altar before fighting <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Antiquated_Plain_Set"},{"id":"antiquated-set","kind":"armor","name":"Antiquated Set","page":"Antiquated Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Antiquated_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":6.361,"strike":6.377,"slash":5.795,"thrust":5.414,"mag":-2.861,"fire":26.372,"ltn":22.484,"dark":24.672},"res":{"bld":47,"psn":86,"fst":61,"cur":202},"weight":7.3,"poise":2.19,"weight_class":"","desc":"Dress sewn in long-lost fashion.\nThe elaborately embroidered, ivory-colored silk is imbued with ancient magic power.\nNo protection is offered by this garment, as it was never intended for battle.","avail":"<p>The Crown of Dusk is found near the Keep Ruins bonfire under the white birch in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>'s poisonous swamp, guarded by a Great Crab.<\/p><p>The dress, gloves, and skirt are located near the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a> found in a cave to the right of the initial bonfire, guarded by several Basilisks.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Antiquated_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"archdeacon-set","kind":"armor","name":"Archdeacon Set","page":"Archdeacon Set","img":"assets/img/Archdeacon_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":7.515,"strike":13.125,"slash":8.936,"thrust":8.936,"mag":23.188,"fire":21.65,"ltn":23.188,"dark":25.3},"res":{"bld":43,"psn":85,"fst":82,"cur":176},"weight":8.6,"poise":7.51,"weight_class":"","desc":"White crown/Holy garb/Skirt worn by an Archdeacon of the Cathedral of the Deep.\n(Crown) Presented solely to delegates of the gods.\nOf the three Archdeacons of the Deep, one cast off his white crown and left the cathedral to stand by Aldrich.\n(Garb) A sign of the Way of White's highest rank.\nOf the three Archdeacons of the Deep, one stood over Aldrich's casket, with hope that he would return one day.\n(Skirt) Worn underneath holy garb.\nOf the three Archdeacons of the Deep, one attended to Rosaria, Mother of Rebirth, whom he deemed a goddess.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>, on Archdeacon Royce's corpse. The body will appear after defeating the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a> and resting at the bonfire.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Archdeacon_Set"},{"id":"assassins-set","kind":"armor","name":"Assassin's Set","page":"Assassin Set","img":"assets/img/Assassin_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":16.699,"strike":16.769,"slash":17.655,"thrust":17.073,"mag":21.179,"fire":23.192,"ltn":19.423,"dark":16.364},"res":{"bld":98,"psn":152,"fst":112,"cur":126},"weight":15,"poise":8.1,"weight_class":"","desc":"Soft leather armor worn by assassins who lurk in the shadows.\nThe thick leather offers reasonable absorption without creating any undesired noise. A well-crafted piece of protection.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment of the Assassin class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for a total of 6,000 souls once he has returned from his first scavenge expedition in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Assassin_Set"},{"id":"black-hand-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Hand Set","page":"Black Hand Set","img":"assets/img/Black_Hand_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":17.655,"strike":14.487,"slash":21.812,"thrust":18.03,"mag":23.83,"fire":24.484,"ltn":19.423,"dark":16.535},"res":{"bld":106,"psn":160,"fst":117,"cur":137},"weight":16.6,"poise":8.29,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of hunters known as the King's Black Hands.\nA black cape covers leather armor, shrouding the wearer in darkness.\nBlack Hand was a title established to honor hunters who served successive kings.\nTo date, no more than three such individuals have borne this distinction.","avail":"<p>The hat and armor are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 7,500 souls after defeating Black Hand Kamui in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<\/p><p>The gloves and trousers are sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for a total of 3,000 souls after he returns from pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. The Shrine Handmaid will also sell them at this price should she be given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Hand_Set"},{"id":"black-iron-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Iron Set","page":"Black Iron Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Iron_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":34.836,"strike":24.282,"slash":35.115,"thrust":34.403,"mag":24.848,"fire":30.867,"ltn":23.437,"dark":25.08},"res":{"bld":157,"psn":118,"fst":133,"cur":86},"weight":36.9,"poise":39.49,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Chest piece made of black iron, from the set of armor for which Knightslayer Tsorig was infamously known.\nOffers extensive and particularly effective protection from fire.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 21,500 souls after defeating Knight Slayer Tsorig in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Iron_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Knight Set","page":"Black Knight Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Knight_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":30.196,"strike":24.042,"slash":28.262,"thrust":26.761,"mag":21.868,"fire":27.641,"ltn":20.767,"dark":23.717},"res":{"bld":141,"psn":100,"fst":95,"cur":95},"weight":30.9,"poise":29.99,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the Black Knights who roam the lands.\nThe Knights served the First Lord Gwyn, and followed him into the flame upon its linking. They became ash, but still wander the realms to this day.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Black Knights in <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>, <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a> and <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Knight_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-leather-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Leather Set","page":"Black Leather Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Leather_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":16.865,"strike":15.691,"slash":17.933,"thrust":13.985,"mag":16.689,"fire":15.605,"ltn":20.17,"dark":16.056},"res":{"bld":108,"psn":148,"fst":125,"cur":102},"weight":13.9,"poise":9.5,"weight_class":"","desc":"Black dyed leather armor. Enables its wearer to hide in the shadows with silent finesse.\nThe wearer of this fine attire was admired by friends and enemies alike, for his skills were unmatched, and his heart was true as gold. As their new owner, you have quite the shoes to fill.","avail":"<ul><li>The head piece is sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 400 souls. If given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> will sell it in his place.<\/li><li>The chest, hands and legs pieces are sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for a total of 6,500 souls. If given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>, the Shrine Handmaid will sell them in his place.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Leather_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Set","page":"Black Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":18.688,"strike":16.991,"slash":22.528,"thrust":16.861,"mag":19.664,"fire":25.352,"ltn":20.837,"dark":24.608},"res":{"bld":109,"psn":127,"fst":104,"cur":150},"weight":18.2,"poise":9.17,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of the three mentors of the Sable Church of Londor.\nThese maidens of a Primordial Serpent were renowned as founders of the Sable Church, which offered salvation for Hollows.\nIt is apparent that the women in black were highly skilled fencers, capable of founding the Sable Church between just the three of them.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 18,000 souls upon <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a>'s death.<\/li><li>Alternatively, the whole set can be found, along with <a data-e=\"darkdrift\">Darkdrift<\/a>, at Yuria's location in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> if she was summoned for and survived the fight against <a data-e=\"soul-of-cinder\">Soul of Cinder<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-witch-set","kind":"armor","name":"Black Witch Set","page":"Black Witch Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Witch_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":8.728,"strike":8.637,"slash":8.637,"thrust":6.734,"mag":27.225,"fire":26.66,"ltn":26.66,"dark":27.787},"res":{"bld":37,"psn":94,"fst":68,"cur":167},"weight":9.2,"poise":1.29,"weight_class":"","desc":"The purple garb of the witch Zullie, who intended to seduce Alva the Wayfarer, but eventually became his closest supporter, spending her entire life with him.\nIt is said that Zullie the witch, who was never loved, nor loved another, experienced all manner of misfortune, and yet in the end, found her purpose in life.","avail":"<ul><li>Armor set with the hat: found on a corpse behind where the dark spirit Alva, Seeker of the Spurned invades in the Ringed City.<\/li><li>Veil: found in the Ringed City Streets area, guarded by a Ringed Knight near the sunken church.<\/li><li>Blindfold Mask: Dropped by the Moaning Knight who invades in the Shared Grave area after first encountering <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Witch_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"brass-set","kind":"armor","name":"Brass Set","page":"Brass Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Brass_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":26.486,"strike":21.678,"slash":26.486,"thrust":23.694,"mag":27.054,"fire":20.483,"ltn":14.517,"dark":20.483},"res":{"bld":145,"psn":80,"fst":88,"cur":66},"weight":25.3,"poise":20.16,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of a knight once known as the Darkmoon. It is said this brass armor hides something hideous within.\nSomething about its silhouette suggests femininity.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, on a corpse within Lord Gwyn's honorary tomb before reaching <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Brass_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"brigand-set","kind":"armor","name":"Brigand Set","page":"Brigand Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Brigand_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":19.518,"strike":17.954,"slash":19.518,"thrust":19.518,"mag":14.492,"fire":16.547,"ltn":18.128,"dark":14.492},"res":{"bld":102,"psn":151,"fst":145,"cur":102},"weight":14.9,"poise":8.16,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor from a foreign land.\nProbably belonged to a brigand who met his match.\nIn foreign lands, undead were banished to send a message to populace, and when the message was not heard, they banished the living, too.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a> bonfire, follow the path toward a stone bridge and from there head to the left and down a narrow path guarded by the madwoman, which leads into a cave where the set is found.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Brigand_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"catarina-set","kind":"armor","name":"Catarina Set","page":"Catarina Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Catarina_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":35.194,"strike":27.769,"slash":35.638,"thrust":34.209,"mag":23.609,"fire":25.268,"ltn":29.133,"dark":26.003},"res":{"bld":184,"psn":141,"fst":141,"cur":85},"weight":40.7,"poise":43.81,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Distinctively shaped armor worn by the Knights of Catarina.\nOften ridiculed for its onion-like shape, infuriating the country's proud knights, but the masterfully forged curved design makes it very effective for deflecting blows.","avail":"<p>Only one set is available per playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward of Catarina<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Siegward upon his death by any cause.<\/li><li>Found in <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a>'s arena upon the completion of Siegward's questline.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a>, after he has stolen the armor from Siegward<ul><li>Purchased from Patches for a total of 15,000 souls. He will sell the set once he is met as a merchant and the double doors on the second level of the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a> (past the elevator near the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a>) have been opened.<\/li><li>Dropped by Patches upon death, if it has not been purchased from him.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Catarina_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"cathedral-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Cathedral Knight Set","page":"Cathedral Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Cathedral_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":32.636,"strike":33.088,"slash":28.956,"thrust":35.166,"mag":27.903,"fire":25.872,"ltn":27.179,"dark":23.904},"res":{"bld":156,"psn":147,"fst":147,"cur":108},"weight":39.2,"poise":41.96,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Massive iron armor worn by knights serving the Cathedral of the Deep.\nRepulsive creatures of the deep are sure to attract the foolish, but the cathedral knights are prepared to meet such intruders head on with their more than ample might.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by Cathedral Knights in <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Consumed King's Knights in <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_Knight_Set"},{"id":"chain-set","kind":"armor","name":"Chain Set","page":"Chain Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Chain_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":21.964,"strike":14.425,"slash":25.946,"thrust":19.911,"mag":18.297,"fire":14.86,"ltn":11.129,"dark":19.596},"res":{"bld":145,"psn":83,"fst":81,"cur":59},"weight":20.3,"poise":14.01,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of thin interlinking rings of steel.\nPopular due to its ease of crafting, respectable damage absorption, and light weight.\nKnights may favor imposing armor, but for warriors on the battlefield, that which keep them alive is armor enough.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 2,300 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Chain_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"cleric-set","kind":"armor","name":"Cleric Set","page":"Cleric Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Cleric_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":9.948,"strike":10.69,"slash":9.437,"thrust":8.356,"mag":25.035,"fire":21.534,"ltn":25.221,"dark":25.536},"res":{"bld":106,"psn":143,"fst":90,"cur":164},"weight":11,"poise":3.07,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb worn by a cleric turned undead.\nUnmistakable vibrant blue robes.\nIt is said that they were entrusted with a duty, still its nature is yet to be revealed.\nThey bore large covers on their backs to ensure they would not become seedbeds for spreading darkness.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment of the Cleric class, excluding the hat.<\/li><li>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. From the Dilapidated Bridge bonfire, head towards the cemetery, then turn left and double back. The set will be on a corpse near a house guarded by a single Thrall.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cleric_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"conjurator-set","kind":"armor","name":"Conjurator Set","page":"Conjurator Set","img":"assets/img/Conjurator_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":8.163,"strike":8.163,"slash":8.163,"thrust":6.931,"mag":23.614,"fire":27.059,"ltn":26.493,"dark":24.605},"res":{"bld":73,"psn":150,"fst":105,"cur":145},"weight":10,"poise":2.77,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of traveling conjurators.\nConjurators were the predecessors to pyromancers, and spent their lives roaming the lands. No wonder their attire was designed to protect them from fire, poison, and other threats of nature.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse near the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome\">Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome<\/a> on the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>, between a large tree and a wall near the Crucifixion Woods bonfire.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Conjurator_Set"},{"id":"cornyxs-set","kind":"armor","name":"Cornyx's Set","page":"Cornyx's Set","img":"assets/img/Cornyx_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":7.326,"strike":7.326,"slash":8.188,"thrust":6.462,"mag":25.042,"fire":25.961,"ltn":24.236,"dark":25.296},"res":{"bld":54,"psn":91,"fst":70,"cur":190},"weight":8.4,"poise":6.98,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of Cornyx, pyromancer of the Great Swamp.\nIn the Great Swamp, it was customary to adorn oneself with articles of nature. Cornyx favored the use of raven feathers.\nRavens are said to have once been Firelink messengers, guiding the undead to the land of ancient gods.","avail":"<ul><li>The head piece is in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>, on the path between the cut bridge and <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>. After defeating or running past the Demon, the player can go into the small hallway to find a corpse at the end holding the blindfold along with the <a data-e=\"witchs-ring\">Witch's Ring<\/a>.<\/li><li>The chest, arm, and leg pieces are all dropped by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> upon death, or found near his cage in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> if the player defeats the <a data-e=\"old-demon-king\">Old Demon King<\/a> with the aid of the Great Swamp Cuculus. Cuculus must survive the fight in order for the set to appear.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cornyx's_Set"},{"id":"court-sorcerer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Court Sorcerer Set","page":"Court Sorcerer Set","img":"assets/img/Court_Sorcerer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":7.504,"strike":8.829,"slash":7.504,"thrust":8.829,"mag":24.612,"fire":23.04,"ltn":26.737,"dark":26.25},"res":{"bld":69,"psn":108,"fst":75,"cur":175},"weight":8.9,"poise":3.27,"weight_class":"","desc":"Robe worn by court sorcerers of the Profaned Capital.\nThe formal gold stitching suggests they may have also been oracles.\nThere are many sorcerers who claim heirship to the great sage \"Big Hat\" Logan, and the Profaned Capital houses one of two leading schools.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/p><p>In the toxic swamp area, climb up the ladder and into the building. The set is located on a corpse next to the central pillar, guarded by a Monstrosity of Sin and Mimic.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Court_Sorcerer_Set"},{"id":"dancers-set","kind":"armor","name":"Dancer's Set","page":"Dancer's Set","img":"assets/img/Dancer_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":20.924,"strike":14.628,"slash":24.437,"thrust":23.363,"mag":16.84,"fire":12.703,"ltn":17.565,"dark":18.96},"res":{"bld":92,"psn":72,"fst":129,"cur":48},"weight":16.9,"poise":12.91,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor worn by the Dancer of the Boreal Valley.\nThe black eyes of the Pontiff eventually transformed the Dancer into a beastly creature, her armor fusing with her own hide.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 31,000 souls after defeating the <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dancer's_Set"},{"id":"dark-set","kind":"armor","name":"Dark Set","page":"Dark Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dark_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":25.743,"strike":19.53,"slash":23.605,"thrust":22.684,"mag":19.873,"fire":16.652,"ltn":9.662,"dark":19.53},"res":{"bld":94,"psn":73,"fst":81,"cur":35},"weight":22.4,"poise":18.85,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of the Darkwraiths, relics of a small country that fell to the dark long ago.\nLooks as if it may crumble to dust at any moment.\nThe Darkwraiths were the oldest of the Red Eye Invaders, and rumored to have served a Primordial Serpent.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the Darkwraiths in <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a> and <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"deacon-set","kind":"armor","name":"Deacon Set","page":"Deacon Set","img":"assets/img/Deacon_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":4.66,"strike":5.239,"slash":6.408,"thrust":5.239,"mag":18.45,"fire":18.724,"ltn":17.169,"dark":19.45},"res":{"bld":32,"psn":66,"fst":55,"cur":129},"weight":5.8,"poise":2.09,"weight_class":"","desc":"Robe worn by deacons of the Cathedral of the Deep.\nThe deep red pigment denotes the blessing of fire.\nIn time, those dedicated to sealing away the horrors of the Deep succumbed to their very power. It seems that neither tending to the flame, nor the faith, could save them.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Deacons in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>, <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> and <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deacon_Set"},{"id":"desert-pyromancer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Desert Pyromancer Set","page":"Desert Pyromancer Set","img":"assets/img/Desert_Pyromancer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":9.839,"strike":6.166,"slash":6.349,"thrust":6.255,"mag":21.499,"fire":23.502,"ltn":24.946,"dark":24.337},"res":{"bld":48,"psn":162,"fst":67,"cur":166},"weight":7,"poise":2.68,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb of the desert pyromancers, who once walked the halls of the Earthen Peak. It is said that the thin, burgundy cloth breathes with magic.\nDesert pyromancers, most of them female, were known for their great fans of flame, and enchanting looks.\nBut what is enchanting can also be deadly, especially when clothed in such alluring garb.","avail":"<p>The pieces are found scattered all throughout the Earthen peak section of <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>:<\/p><ul><li>The Garb is found shortly after the <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">Earthen Peak Ruins<\/a> bonfire, to the left of the initial area guarded by the second Angel. It is on the opposite side of a ruined house, guarded by two Thralls.<\/li><li>The Gloves are located on the right-hand side of the Poison swamp area, on a stone ramp that is within the third Angel's patrol area.<\/li><li>The Skirt is located next to the Gloves, within the swamp itself and guarded by several Poisonhorn Bugs.<\/li><li>The Hood is found at the very top of the area, on the cliffside where Desert Pyromancer Zoey is fought and before traversing the tree branches.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Desert_Pyromancer_Set"},{"id":"deserter-set","kind":"armor","name":"Deserter Set","page":"Deserter Set","img":"assets/img/Deserter_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":19.131,"strike":16.848,"slash":19.131,"thrust":18.411,"mag":13.843,"fire":14.673,"ltn":11.655,"dark":19.755},"res":{"bld":98,"psn":85,"fst":82,"cur":60},"weight":16.3,"poise":13.38,"weight_class":"","desc":"Common soldier's armor.\nIts insignia is worn beyond recognition.\nThis musty, rusted hunk of metal befits one reduced to thievery.","avail":"<ul><li>The Deserter Armor and Deserter Trousers are the starting equipment of the Thief class.<\/li><li>Dropped by Hollow Soldiers.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deserter_Set"},{"id":"dragonscale-set","kind":"armor","name":"Dragonscale Set","page":"Dragonscale Set","img":"assets/img/Dragonscale_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":25.084,"strike":21.829,"slash":23.686,"thrust":19.925,"mag":19.263,"fire":25.19,"ltn":14.102,"dark":19.263},"res":{"bld":124,"psn":111,"fst":112,"cur":78},"weight":23.7,"poise":24.78,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of a nameless king who was ally to the ancient dragons.\nThe golden crown, buried amidst long strands of bristling ash, is said to closely resemble that of the First Lord.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 36,000 souls after <a data-e=\"the-nameless-king\">The Nameless King<\/a> is defeated.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonscale_Set"},{"id":"dragonslayer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Dragonslayer Set","page":"Dragonslayer Set","img":"assets/img/Dragonslayer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":29.041,"strike":23.99,"slash":31.475,"thrust":31.475,"mag":24.001,"fire":25.886,"ltn":25.886,"dark":19.683},"res":{"bld":151,"psn":94,"fst":99,"cur":85},"weight":31.6,"poise":34.3,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Golden lion armor associated with Dragonslayer Ornstein, from the age of gods, and imbued with the strength of lightning.\nIn the dragonless age, this knight, who long guarded the ruined cathedral, left the land in search of the nameless king.","avail":"<p>Found on the far side of the courtyard below <a data-e=\"the-nameless-king\">The Nameless King<\/a>'s arena, after defeating the Nameless King.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonslayer_Set"},{"id":"drakeblood-set","kind":"armor","name":"Drakeblood Set","page":"Drakeblood Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Drakeblood_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":27.709,"strike":27.395,"slash":32.491,"thrust":26.581,"mag":25.693,"fire":24.625,"ltn":22.791,"dark":22.791},"res":{"bld":182,"psn":98,"fst":106,"cur":74},"weight":32.9,"poise":31.59,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the Drakeblood Knights, worshippers of the blood of dragons. The red cloth is said to symbolize their yearning for blood.\nDragon worship has captured the hearts and minds of warriors across the lands for many ages. Perhaps such warriors are attracted to doctrines of few words.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>, on the corpse that teaches the Path of the Dragon gesture. For it to appear, the player must first defeat at least one Drakeblood Knight at <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Drakeblood_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"drang-set","kind":"armor","name":"Drang Set","page":"Drang Set","img":"assets/img/Drang_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":15.378,"strike":14.999,"slash":13.987,"thrust":11.399,"mag":17.081,"fire":13.355,"ltn":19.043,"dark":17.081},"res":{"bld":79,"psn":118,"fst":126,"cur":85},"weight":11,"poise":2.38,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of the Drang Knights, proclaimed descendants of the land known for the legend of the Linking of the Fire.\nFine protection that is both light and strong, having been reinforced with rare geisteel.\nThe Drang knights were once feared sellswords, until treason meant descending into the abyss, and they were separated forever.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>, in the murky waters near the staircase that leads to the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a>. It is guarded by a Giant Slave, several Writhing Rotten Flesh and a Man-grub.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Drang_Set"},{"id":"eastern-armor-set","kind":"armor","name":"Eastern Armor Set","page":"Eastern Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Eastern_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":22.685,"strike":17.578,"slash":30.194,"thrust":20.728,"mag":15.536,"fire":23.124,"ltn":13.922,"dark":14.714},"res":{"bld":191,"psn":98,"fst":110,"cur":80},"weight":22.6,"poise":21.22,"weight_class":"","desc":"Distinctive armor made in an Eastern land.\nThe exquisite craftsmanship and artistic design made these prized pieces in the collection of any nobleman.\nOffers excellent damage absorption, particularly from slashing attacks from katanas, which are commonly encountered threats in battles fought in the East.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 23,000 souls after giving her the <a data-e=\"easterners-ashes\">Easterner's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Eastern_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"elite-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Elite Knight Set","page":"Elite Knight Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Elite_Knight_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":25.952,"strike":20.952,"slash":26.028,"thrust":24.056,"mag":20.789,"fire":23.072,"ltn":16.712,"dark":19.59},"res":{"bld":126,"psn":85,"fst":88,"cur":52},"weight":24.3,"poise":21.03,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor said to have been given to elite knights of fallen Astora.\nThe mere mention of Astora invoked wistful pangs, and perhaps it was such a dream that drew Anri to this faraway home known only by name.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 13,500 souls upon the death of <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a>, either from the completion of <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a>'s questline or from killing Anri.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Elite_Knight_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"evangelist-set","kind":"armor","name":"Evangelist Set","page":"Evangelist Set","img":"assets/img/Evangelist_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":22.717,"strike":24.511,"slash":21.539,"thrust":19.259,"mag":22.283,"fire":24.785,"ltn":23.152,"dark":15.696},"res":{"bld":99,"psn":130,"fst":116,"cur":118},"weight":22.4,"poise":18.19,"weight_class":"","desc":"Robe of an evangelist sent from the cathedral.\nThese teachers, all women, came to enlighten inhabitants of the Undead Settlement and sent carriers on the path of sacrifice.","avail":"<p>Drops from the Evangelists in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a> and <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Evangelist_Set"},{"id":"executioner-set","kind":"armor","name":"Executioner Set","page":"Executioner Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Executioner_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":34.989,"strike":24.612,"slash":33.985,"thrust":34.296,"mag":26.737,"fire":28.041,"ltn":22.699,"dark":26.174},"res":{"bld":159,"psn":143,"fst":150,"cur":105},"weight":38,"poise":39.98,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Steel armor of Horace the Hushed, who took a liking to its cold, bulky insides.\nThe original owner was said to be a corrupt executioner, who was killed and stripped of his armor.\nHorace is one of only two children to escape Aldrich's clutches.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 18,000 souls after <a data-e=\"horace-the-hushed\">Horace the Hushed<\/a> is killed.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Executioner_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"exile-set","kind":"armor","name":"Exile Set","page":"Exile Set","img":"assets/img/Exile_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":35.052,"strike":33.865,"slash":32.907,"thrust":31.093,"mag":25.011,"fire":28.262,"ltn":24.637,"dark":25.83},"res":{"bld":226,"psn":171,"fst":143,"cur":114},"weight":40.3,"poise":43.17,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the watchdogs of Farron's Keep.\nAfter the Legion's Watchers became Lords of Cinder, the wolf blood dried up, and Farron was consumed by a festering wood.\nWithin the wood, an emaciated old wolf commands watchdogs to defend the sanctity of sleeping warriors.\nBoth the exiles were surely watchdogs themselves, for Farron has always been a land of itinerants.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 13,500 souls once the player has defeated the two Exile Watchdogs in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a> who guard the way to the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Exile_Set"},{"id":"fallen-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Fallen Knight Set","page":"Fallen Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Fallen_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":25.343,"strike":24.516,"slash":20.228,"thrust":22.435,"mag":17.612,"fire":25.573,"ltn":21.414,"dark":18.084},"res":{"bld":97,"psn":57,"fst":88,"cur":47},"weight":22.2,"poise":17.97,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of an order of fallen knights who disbanded and fled, but met untimely deaths.\nThe drab, tattered cloth conceals tough, black metal which provides dependable protection from fire.\nIt is just possible to make out the majestic gold engravings on its surface.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>. In the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Crucifixion Woods<\/a> swamp area, it is found on a corpse before the ladder to <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, where the two Exile Watchdogs stand guard.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fallen_Knight_Set"},{"id":"faraam-set","kind":"armor","name":"Faraam Set","page":"Faraam Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Faraam_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":27.289,"strike":27.438,"slash":27.289,"thrust":25.259,"mag":21.664,"fire":24.028,"ltn":22.264,"dark":22.264},"res":{"bld":141,"psn":102,"fst":147,"cur":67},"weight":30.4,"poise":32.57,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor named after a god of war.\nThe armor of the Forossa Lion Knights was preserved even after the destruction of their homeland, and is mentioned in numerous legends, alongside the names of those who are said to have gone beyond death.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 18,000 souls after defeating Lion Knight Albert in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Faraam_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"fire-keeper-set","kind":"armor","name":"Fire Keeper Set","page":"Fire Keeper Set","img":"assets/img/Fire_Keeper_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":8.232,"strike":10.33,"slash":9.868,"thrust":10.38,"mag":16.371,"fire":21.282,"ltn":17.467,"dark":22.563},"res":{"bld":58,"psn":93,"fst":78,"cur":105},"weight":8.5,"poise":2.59,"weight_class":"","desc":"Robe worn by the guardian of the shrine.\nThe Fire Keepers were robbed of light, to better serve as vessels for souls. Only those who cherish the writhing, searing darkness were given the keepers' black attire.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse by dropping off the bridge in front of the lift in the tower containing the <a data-e=\"fire-keeper-soul\">Fire Keeper Soul<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/p><p>Instead of jumping safely to the casket on the right (when looking at the lift), look to the left of the bridge and there will be a dead body visible below. Jumping toward it will most likely make the player miss their footing and sustain massive fall damage as a consequence, killing them even at maxed out Vigor and with the <a data-e=\"silvercat-ring\">Silvercat Ring<\/a> equipped. It's recommended just to run off instead of jumping.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Keeper_Set"},{"id":"fire-witch-set","kind":"armor","name":"Fire Witch Set","page":"Fire Witch Set","img":"assets/img/Fire_Witch_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":25.546,"strike":14.941,"slash":20.763,"thrust":20.601,"mag":23.075,"fire":24.216,"ltn":16.078,"dark":21.543},"res":{"bld":104,"psn":73,"fst":83,"cur":60},"weight":22.9,"poise":18.39,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of witches who bore the Profaned Flame, now harrowed spirits of Irithyll.\nThe witches who lead the Pontiff's Knights were originally ordained as holy knights. It was not long however, before their hearts were swallowed by the Profaned Flame.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Fire Witches in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> and <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Witch_Set"},{"id":"firelink-set","kind":"armor","name":"Firelink Set","page":"Firelink Set","img":"assets/img/Firelink_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":22.483,"strike":16.575,"slash":24.322,"thrust":19.572,"mag":17.319,"fire":23.473,"ltn":16.372,"dark":14.24},"res":{"bld":111,"psn":104,"fst":127,"cur":85},"weight":20.2,"poise":16.96,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of the Soul of Cinder, a deific manifestation of the Lords of Cinder, who linked the First Flame.\nIt resembles a knight's armor, but bears hideous burns and contortions.\nIt exists as a symbol of the great Lords and the noble act of linking the fire, though it is no more than an empty husk.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 40,000 souls after defeating the <a data-e=\"soul-of-cinder\">Soul of Cinder<\/a>.<\/p><p>It is not required to enter NG+ in order to buy it, although if bought in NG, a second Firelink Set will become available in NG+.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Firelink_Set"},{"id":"follower-set","kind":"armor","name":"Follower Set","page":"Follower Set","img":"assets/img/Follower_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":16.014,"strike":20.822,"slash":17.602,"thrust":20.204,"mag":20.327,"fire":17.809,"ltn":20.714,"dark":17.554},"res":{"bld":93,"psn":129,"fst":148,"cur":104},"weight":14.3,"poise":7.69,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor worn by the Farron Followers.\nWhen a warrior of Farron fell to the Abyss, the tall, lean Followers, with their hollowed eyes, quietly appeared in groups to hunt them down.\nFarron and its Watchers fell to ruin, but the Followers survived as a wandering pack of Hollows.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Farron Followers in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Follower_Set"},{"id":"grave-warden-set","kind":"armor","name":"Grave Warden Set","page":"Grave Warden Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Grave_Warden_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":8.168,"strike":6.17,"slash":16.139,"thrust":9.762,"mag":17.819,"fire":17.819,"ltn":21.782,"dark":7.126},"res":{"bld":155,"psn":145,"fst":35,"cur":127},"weight":8.5,"poise":1.79,"weight_class":"","desc":"Rotting, tattered robe. Attire of grave wardens at the Cathedral of the Deep.\nGrave wardens were tasked with disposing of the ever rising corpses that plagued the cathedral. Their clothes are utterly putrid, drenched in the blood and mucilage of their undertaking.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Grave Wardens in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a> and <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Grave_Warden_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"gundyrs-set","kind":"armor","name":"Gundyr's Set","page":"Gundyr's Set","img":"assets/img/Gundyr_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":31.972,"strike":27.08,"slash":36.713,"thrust":30.66,"mag":25.532,"fire":26.431,"ltn":25.28,"dark":25.532},"res":{"bld":198,"psn":144,"fst":144,"cur":144},"weight":40,"poise":44.37,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Ancient chest piece of a set of cast iron armor, belonging to Champion Gundyr.\nGundyr, or the Belated Champion, was bested by an unknown warrior. He then became sheath to a coiled sword in the hopes that someday, the first flame would be linked once more.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 36,000 souls after defeating <a data-e=\"champion-gundyr\">Champion Gundyr<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Gundyr's_Set"},{"id":"harald-legion-set","kind":"armor","name":"Harald Legion Set","page":"Harald Legion Set","img":"assets/img/Harald_Legion_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":28.669,"strike":26.679,"slash":29.155,"thrust":28.814,"mag":20.615,"fire":20.792,"ltn":20.319,"dark":22.504},"res":{"bld":118,"psn":118,"fst":112,"cur":114},"weight":29.9,"poise":31.28,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor worn by the Harald Legion, who sought the dark soul.\nThe armor sank into the dark with the legion, where their cavities bloated in grotesque displays, never again to fit any ordinarily-shaped body.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Harald Legion Knights.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Harald_Legion_Set"},{"id":"hard-leather-set","kind":"armor","name":"Hard Leather Set","page":"Hard Leather Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Hard_Leather_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":19.746,"strike":20.611,"slash":19.746,"thrust":19.746,"mag":16.344,"fire":17.841,"ltn":12.656,"dark":16.344},"res":{"bld":111,"psn":153,"fst":142,"cur":122},"weight":18.7,"poise":12.47,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor made of thick, layered leather.\nUsed by warriors of old, but one can still expect sound defense.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for a total of 6,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hard_Leather_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"havels-set","kind":"armor","name":"Havel's Set","page":"Havel's Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Havel_s_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":35.288,"strike":32.724,"slash":35.068,"thrust":33.563,"mag":27.63,"fire":31.266,"ltn":25.352,"dark":27.63},"res":{"bld":172,"psn":165,"fst":165,"cur":145},"weight":56.9,"poise":50.15,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor as if hewn from a giant boulder. Highly protective, but excessively heavy.\nThe warriors who followed Havel the Rock never flinched, nor retreated from battle, crushing any foe that stood in their way.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse in the area guarded by the Stray Demon on the bridge above the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Old Wolf of Farron<\/a> bonfire.<\/p><p>The corpse will only appear after defeating Havel the Rock at the top of <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>. Defeating the version summoned by the Man Serpent Summoner will not cause the set to appear.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Havel's_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"herald-set","kind":"armor","name":"Herald Set","page":"Herald Set","img":"assets/img/Herald_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":24.454,"strike":17.892,"slash":24.8,"thrust":23.215,"mag":17.83,"fire":17.186,"ltn":7.694,"dark":16.242},"res":{"bld":118,"psn":76,"fst":85,"cur":48},"weight":20.5,"poise":18.36,"weight_class":"","desc":"Steel armor with a pure white cape, the signature of Heralds of the Way of White.\nProtection made of steel has excellent physical absorption, but is found lacking against blunt strikes and lightning damage.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Herald class.<\/li><li>Found on the path after the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> arena that leads to the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>. The set may be found on a corpse in a clearing, guarded by an Evangelist next to a large bonfire.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Herald_Set"},{"id":"iron-dragonslayer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Iron Dragonslayer Set","page":"Iron Dragonslayer Set","img":"assets/img/Iron_Dragonslayer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":31.013,"strike":23.611,"slash":32.328,"thrust":33.549,"mag":20.484,"fire":23.611,"ltn":27.618,"dark":26.49},"res":{"bld":188,"psn":125,"fst":138,"cur":64},"weight":35.7,"poise":38.1,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Stark melted iron body armor of the ancient Dragonslayer Armour.\nThe Armour, defeated by the Champion of Ash in Lothric, was left ages to rust, until it slipped into an abyssal swamp, where it was possessed once again by the memory of the hunt.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the Iron Dragonslayer in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">the Ringed City<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Iron_Dragonslayer_Set"},{"id":"iron-set","kind":"armor","name":"Iron Set","page":"Iron Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Iron_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":22.441,"strike":18.311,"slash":22.278,"thrust":22.278,"mag":21.254,"fire":21.254,"ltn":20.055,"dark":21.254},"res":{"bld":83,"psn":71,"fst":77,"cur":66},"weight":22.3,"poise":24.16,"weight_class":"","desc":"Chainmail armor and white coat featuring a large rendition of the holy symbol of the sun.\nThe choice attire of a singular Knight of Sunlight from a previous age. The symbol was painted by the knight himself, but the armor never bore any special power, sacred or otherwise.","avail":"<p>Trading the following items with Pickle Pee will net all four armor pieces:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"lightning-urn\">Lightning Urn<\/a> gives the Iron Helm.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"siegbr-u\">Siegbräu<\/a> gives the Armor of the Sun.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"homeward-bone\">Homeward Bone<\/a> gives the Iron Bracelets.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"seed-of-a-giant-tree\">Seed of a Giant Tree<\/a> gives the Iron Leggings.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Iron_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"jailer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Jailer Set","page":"Jailer Set","img":"assets/img/Jailer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":18.738,"strike":9.198,"slash":18.565,"thrust":14.783,"mag":24.855,"fire":24.426,"ltn":20.331,"dark":24.699},"res":{"bld":71,"psn":91,"fst":81,"cur":200},"weight":14.9,"poise":9.85,"weight_class":"","desc":"Robe worn by the jailers of Irithyll Dungeon.\nOriginally ritualistic formal wear.\nThe jailers were among the few survivors inhabiting the Profaned Capital, later serving under Pontiff Sulyvahn.\nPerhaps the screams emanating from the cells help them forget their old home.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Jailers in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Jailer_Set"},{"id":"karlas-set","kind":"armor","name":"Karla's Set","page":"Karla's Set","img":"assets/img/Karla_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":8.633,"strike":8.54,"slash":8.54,"thrust":6.735,"mag":27.787,"fire":26.254,"ltn":27.225,"dark":27.225},"res":{"bld":50,"psn":85,"fst":75,"cur":130},"weight":9.1,"poise":3.07,"weight_class":"","desc":"Coat of the dark witch Karla.\nThis stained coat is torn and odorous, telling of a long journey and even longer imprisonment.\nIt would be madness to wear such a thing.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 23,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"prisoner-chiefs-ashes\">Prisoner Chief's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Karla's_Set"},{"id":"knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Knight Set","page":"Knight Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Knight_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":27.914,"strike":23.847,"slash":27.914,"thrust":26.634,"mag":18.047,"fire":22.181,"ltn":15.036,"dark":18.216},"res":{"bld":107,"psn":88,"fst":89,"cur":56},"weight":25.8,"poise":24.88,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of a lowly knight, fashioned from solid iron.\nThis iron armor might be on the heftier side compared to others of its ilk, but as such offers great physical absorption in exchange for its imposing weight.\nDo not think to wear it without the necessary Vitality.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Knight class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for a total of 10,000 souls once he returns from his first pillaging journey.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Knight_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lapps-set","kind":"armor","name":"Lapp's Set","page":"Lapp's Set","img":"assets/img/Lapp_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":35.124,"strike":30.466,"slash":35.124,"thrust":35.052,"mag":24.765,"fire":25.505,"ltn":22.769,"dark":24.765},"res":{"bld":178,"psn":141,"fst":125,"cur":86},"weight":36.9,"poise":39.11,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Steel armor of the amnesiac Lapp.\nThis plate-armor body, that covers the torso cleanly without even slight gaps, provides heavy defense.\nQuite fit to conceal a hollowed body, and indeed, one's very identity.","avail":"<ul><li>Left by <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a> at his final meeting place in the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Shared Grave<\/a>, at the end of his questline.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 31,000 souls if the player kills Lapp.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lapp's_Set"},{"id":"leather-set","kind":"armor","name":"Leather Set","page":"Leather Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Leather_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":14.341,"strike":13.901,"slash":14.341,"thrust":14.341,"mag":18.05,"fire":19.437,"ltn":20.724,"dark":18.05},"res":{"bld":88,"psn":139,"fst":136,"cur":104},"weight":12.5,"poise":7.42,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor made of smooth leather. Even lighter and more flexible than most leather armors.","avail":"<ul><li>The armor, gloves and boots are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 1,800 souls after giving her the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>The hat can be obtained as a guaranteed drop from one of the three Elder Ghrus located near the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Keep Ruins<\/a> bonfire in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Leather_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"leonhards-set","kind":"armor","name":"Leonhard's Set","page":"Leonhard's Set","img":"assets/img/Leonhard_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":18.613,"strike":20.206,"slash":18.149,"thrust":19.037,"mag":23.228,"fire":24.461,"ltn":19.204,"dark":16.226},"res":{"bld":93,"psn":128,"fst":142,"cur":128},"weight":16.6,"poise":11.62,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb of Ringfinger Leonhard.\nLeonhard was born into royalty, which is believed to be the reason for his skill in both sorcery and swordsmanship.\nIndeed, this dingy garb is in fact embroidered with gold thread, betraying its purpose as military wear designed for a noble.","avail":"<p>The mask is dropped by <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Ringfinger Leonhard<\/a> upon death. The remaining pieces are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 10,500 souls after Leonhard is killed.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Leonhard's_Set"},{"id":"lorians-set","kind":"armor","name":"Lorian's Set","page":"Lorian's Set","img":"assets/img/Lorian_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":29.891,"strike":20.243,"slash":29.746,"thrust":27.334,"mag":25.786,"fire":20.065,"ltn":20.065,"dark":26.123},"res":{"bld":145,"psn":81,"fst":116,"cur":100},"weight":30.1,"poise":28.37,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of Prince Lothric's older brother Lorian. This black-dyed brass armor was passed down to him from the royal family.\nLorian, raised as a knight, is said to have been left mute and crippled by his younger brother's curse. It is also said that Lorian, in fact, wished it so.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 45,000 souls after <a data-e=\"lorian-elder-prince-and-lothric-younger-prince\">Lorian, Elder Prince and Lothric, Younger Prince<\/a> have been defeated.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lorian's_Set"},{"id":"lothric-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Lothric Knight Set","page":"Lothric Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Lothric_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":30.135,"strike":23.895,"slash":34.79,"thrust":28.947,"mag":24.627,"fire":26.679,"ltn":19.576,"dark":22.976},"res":{"bld":175,"psn":100,"fst":131,"cur":80},"weight":34.5,"poise":37.7,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of a celebrated Lothric knight.\nThe coat of distinction is all but fallen apart.\nThe Knight has served as one of the Three Pillars since ancient times, and shares place alongside the wyverns as a symbol of Lothric.\nOnly those possessing a knight's resolve are fit to wear this garment.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Lothric Knights in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>, <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>, <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a> and <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lothric_Knight_Set"},{"id":"maiden-set","kind":"armor","name":"Maiden Set","page":"Maiden Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Maiden_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":6.934,"strike":8.167,"slash":6.934,"thrust":6.169,"mag":26.51,"fire":24.952,"ltn":25.36,"dark":26.51},"res":{"bld":48,"psn":93,"fst":73,"cur":180},"weight":8.5,"poise":1.1,"weight_class":"","desc":"White robe worn by traveling maidens.\nPart of their formal attire, regardless of rank.\nIt is soft and well-made, but ill-suited for use in battle.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>, at the feet of a Giant Slave in the murky pool farthest away from the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Maiden_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"masters-set","kind":"armor","name":"Master's Set","page":"Master's Set","img":"assets/img/Master_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":5.976,"strike":5.796,"slash":5.796,"thrust":5.012,"mag":19.191,"fire":16.215,"ltn":17.801,"dark":19.191},"res":{"bld":84,"psn":144,"fst":48,"cur":172},"weight":4.1,"poise":0.8,"weight_class":"","desc":"A terribly worn shirt.\nMen are fond of weaving tales to explain the raggedness of their garb.\nMy sixth sense warned me of danger, and I danced between flurries of blades, unscathed, but alas, my clothes went to tatters.","avail":"<ul><li>The Attire and Gloves are dropped by the Sword Master outside of <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/li><li>The Mask is found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, to the left of the initial bonfire guarded by Rotten Slugs.<\/li><li>The Loincloth is found in <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, next to the <a data-e=\"velka-the-goddess-of-sin\">Statue of Velka<\/a>; it requires the <a data-e=\"grave-key\">Grave Key<\/a> to obtain. Alternatively, it is the starting equipment for the Deprived class.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Master's_Set"},{"id":"millwood-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Millwood Knight Set","page":"Millwood Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Millwood_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":34.989,"strike":27.307,"slash":33.563,"thrust":29.776,"mag":25.603,"fire":24.944,"ltn":25.603,"dark":24.944},"res":{"bld":159,"psn":145,"fst":165,"cur":88},"weight":37.3,"poise":38.12,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor worn by knights of Millwood. The charbronze breastplate and the thick black cape are adorned with the symbol of the Ethereal Oak.\nWhen the fabled Millwood forest was discovered it was a vacant ruin. The only thing left was the Ethereal Oak, stood rotting. No corpses were discovered, yet their belongings lay neatly on the ground.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 23,500 souls after giving her the <a data-e=\"captains-ashes\">Captain's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Millwood_Knight_Set"},{"id":"mirrah-chain-set","kind":"armor","name":"Mirrah Chain Set","page":"Mirrah Chain Set","img":"assets/img/Mirrah_Chain_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":24.542,"strike":20,"slash":28.971,"thrust":20.665,"mag":22.056,"fire":21.859,"ltn":13.824,"dark":18.325},"res":{"bld":127,"psn":88,"fst":95,"cur":67},"weight":25.3,"poise":23.91,"weight_class":"","desc":"Formal attire of the honorable knights of Mirrah, featuring their heraldry, a stag set against a blue field.\nOddly, it was a dishonorable deserter who wore this attire most religiously.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. After defeating Creighton of Mirrah when he invades in the graveyard past the Church of Yorshka bonfire, return to the bridge that leads into Central Irithyll. The set can be found on a corpse in the middle of the bridge where Creighton was first fought.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Mirrah_Chain_Set"},{"id":"mirrah-set","kind":"armor","name":"Mirrah Set","page":"Mirrah Set","img":"assets/img/Mirrah_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":20.091,"strike":19.842,"slash":15.535,"thrust":15.361,"mag":20.016,"fire":18.717,"ltn":24.241,"dark":18.717},"res":{"bld":122,"psn":148,"fst":122,"cur":135},"weight":15.9,"poise":7.05,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb worn by Mirrah Knights sent on journeys. This hard leather vest is bestowed only upon proven knights.\nKnights travel afar to fulfill their sacred duties, but few are ever able to deliver on their vows.","avail":"<ul><li>Set without Lucatiel's Mask can be found on a corpse in a tower along with the <a data-e=\"chloranthy-ring\">Chloranthy Ring<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. The tower is accessible by dropping down off the rooftop where two Evangelists guard <a data-e=\"flynns-ring\">Flynn's Ring<\/a>.<\/li><li>Lucatiel's Mask is obtained by trading a <a data-e=\"vertebra-shackle\">Vertebra Shackle<\/a> with Pickle Pee at <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Mirrah_Set"},{"id":"mornes-set","kind":"armor","name":"Morne's Set","page":"Morne's Set","img":"assets/img/Morne_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":33.2,"strike":28.184,"slash":33.2,"thrust":32.108,"mag":27.544,"fire":27.056,"ltn":26.493,"dark":18.859},"res":{"bld":159,"psn":91,"fst":141,"cur":87},"weight":37.3,"poise":38.91,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Black armor bestowed upon knights of Carim.\nModeled on Morne, the Archbishop's apostle, cast from a unique mineral resembling stone.\nA Carim knight will dedicate an entire career to attending a single maiden, just as Morne once served one goddess alone.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 23,000 souls after completing <a data-e=\"eygon-of-carim\">Eygon of Carim<\/a>'s questline. The Shrine Handmaid will also sell it should the player kill Eygon.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Morne's_Set"},{"id":"nameless-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Nameless Knight Set","page":"Nameless Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Nameless_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":23.371,"strike":20.154,"slash":25.273,"thrust":22.361,"mag":15.779,"fire":22.44,"ltn":17.371,"dark":15.779},"res":{"bld":142,"psn":85,"fst":78,"cur":48},"weight":21.5,"poise":17.91,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of a nameless knight. Crafted with thin metal greatly reinforced by a grooved finish.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. From the Keep Ruins bonfire, head towards the gate that leads towards the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a> mausoleum and turn right, following along the wall within the swamp. In the deep swamp zone, the set can be found inside a crevice where the wall ends and an impassable cliff begins.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Nameless_Knight_Set"},{"id":"northern-set","kind":"armor","name":"Northern Set","page":"Northern Set","img":"assets/img/Northern_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":23.59,"strike":25.27,"slash":22.991,"thrust":22.391,"mag":13.672,"fire":22.609,"ltn":13.242,"dark":12.561},"res":{"bld":123,"psn":104,"fst":156,"cur":88},"weight":22,"poise":17.51,"weight_class":"","desc":"Iron armor of a stalwart northern warrior. Supported by interwoven chainmail.\nIron defensive wear grants superior absorption. Being from the north, it should also offer resistance to the cold.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Warrior class.<\/li><li>Found on a hanging corpse in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, at the same area where the Demon is fought alongside <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward of Catarina<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Northern_Set"},{"id":"old-sorcerer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Old Sorcerer Set","page":"Old Sorcerer Set","img":"assets/img/Old_Sorcerer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":7.877,"strike":6.833,"slash":6.833,"thrust":7.877,"mag":25.501,"fire":23.358,"ltn":24.352,"dark":25.501},"res":{"bld":72,"psn":92,"fst":79,"cur":164},"weight":8.5,"poise":2.68,"weight_class":"","desc":"Traditional attire worn by sorcerers of the Vinheim Dragon School.\nLong ago, sorcerers were said to always dress properly, even while on distant journeys of discovery, even before such journeys were established curriculum.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>. In the initial cell block, navigate down to the lower level and enter the first cell encountered. The set will be found in this cell, guarded by four Infested Corpses.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Old_Sorcerer_Set"},{"id":"ordained-set","kind":"armor","name":"Ordained Set","page":"Ordained Set","img":"assets/img/Ordained_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":10.543,"strike":7.33,"slash":14.6,"thrust":5.409,"mag":25.673,"fire":20.473,"ltn":22.624,"dark":22.543},"res":{"bld":41,"psn":105,"fst":99,"cur":144},"weight":9.1,"poise":4.64,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb of Friede, Sister of the Painted World. A light blue dress sewn with thin fabric.\nAfter renouncing everything, Friede discovered a people that she wished to protect, and assumed the precise form that they yearned for.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 33,000 souls once <a data-e=\"sister-friede\">Sister Friede<\/a> has been defeated.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ordained_Set"},{"id":"outrider-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Outrider Knight Set","page":"Outrider Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Outrider_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":27.194,"strike":20.277,"slash":26.214,"thrust":26.683,"mag":18.974,"fire":22.302,"ltn":18.63,"dark":13.312},"res":{"bld":111,"psn":89,"fst":203,"cur":45},"weight":25.5,"poise":23.2,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of an Irithyll outrider knight.\nEnveloped in a dimly cool air.\nThe knights were given the eyes of the Pontiff, but the eyes transformed them into savage, raving warriors who only knew how to serve as mindless guards.","avail":"<p>Guaranteed drop from the Boreal Outrider Knight in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>. The knight is located inside a hidden room behind an illusory wall on the fourth floor, on an alcove on the left wing.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Outrider_Knight_Set"},{"id":"painting-guardian-set","kind":"armor","name":"Painting Guardian Set","page":"Painting Guardian Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Painting_Guardian_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":10.223,"strike":7.785,"slash":10.223,"thrust":11.432,"mag":22.441,"fire":11.897,"ltn":11.243,"dark":9.665},"res":{"bld":147,"psn":157,"fst":81,"cur":128},"weight":10.6,"poise":5.44,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of the Painting Guardians, whose forms are described in the mythology of heretics.\nA smooth pale gown that deters magic.\nThe hunchbacked teller of ancient tales describes unwanted souls who are unwelcome across the lands, and are eventually drawn into a cold, painted world.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse while dropping down the Prison Tower from platform to platform in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>, where Captain Yorshka resides.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Painting_Guardian_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"pale-shade-set","kind":"armor","name":"Pale Shade Set","page":"Pale Shade Set","img":"assets/img/Pale_Shade_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":8.263,"strike":8.542,"slash":8.263,"thrust":6.455,"mag":25.156,"fire":24.553,"ltn":21.674,"dark":21.811},"res":{"bld":99,"psn":140,"fst":80,"cur":155},"weight":8.9,"poise":3.66,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire worn by those who kill in the name of the Sable Church of Londor.\nThe Pale Shades of the Sable Church are all undying Hollows, giving rise to much fear and contempt.\nTheir fight is one of neither honor nor exaltation, yielding nothing but withered moans.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> after defeating the Londor Pale Shade in both of his invasions. The set can be found near <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a>'s corpse.<\/p><p>The availability requires structured events to occur:<\/p><ol><li>Displease or kill <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> at <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/li><li>Find and defeat the Londor Pale Shade in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Find and defeat the Londor Pale Shade in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/li><\/ol>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pale_Shade_Set"},{"id":"pontiff-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Pontiff Knight Set","page":"Pontiff Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Pontiff_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":18.093,"strike":10.613,"slash":18.093,"thrust":16.687,"mag":26.063,"fire":19.272,"ltn":24.178,"dark":26.869},"res":{"bld":92,"psn":82,"fst":188,"cur":65},"weight":16.5,"poise":11.09,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of the Pontiff's Knights, now harrowed spirits of Irithyll.\nThis blue-gray armor, shrouded in a thinly cold air, is light and brittle.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Pontiff Knights in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pontiff_Knight_Set"},{"id":"prayer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Prayer Set","page":"Prayer Set","img":"assets/img/Prayer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":5.901,"strike":5.799,"slash":5.901,"thrust":5.319,"mag":22.609,"fire":21.76,"ltn":21.922,"dark":24.562},"res":{"bld":35,"psn":128,"fst":55,"cur":187},"weight":6.7,"poise":1.5,"weight_class":"","desc":"The prince, destined to be a Lord of Cinder, was cherished by the royal family, despite being born into illness, a frail and shriveled child.\nHis swaddling clothes were made of aged, coarse cloth used in ancient prayer, and are all that he has ever worn.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a> bonfires, head into the next room and it can be found in a chest to the right.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Prayer_Set"},{"id":"pyromancer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Pyromancer Set","page":"Pyromancer Set","img":"assets/img/Pyromancer_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":8.925,"strike":7.787,"slash":7.6,"thrust":7.6,"mag":24.423,"fire":26.709,"ltn":24.277,"dark":26.705},"res":{"bld":51,"psn":121,"fst":95,"cur":164},"weight":9.4,"poise":2.87,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of pyromancers of the Great Swamp. Comprised of bronze ornamentation and animal pelt.\nIn the Great Swamp, bronze was used ritualistically to ward off evil spirits and keep darkness at bay.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Pyromancer Class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for a total of 2,300 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pyromancer_Set"},{"id":"ringed-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Ringed Knight Set","page":"Ringed Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Ringed_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":25.67,"strike":20.212,"slash":28.194,"thrust":24.593,"mag":22.183,"fire":25.689,"ltn":24.11,"dark":19.961},"res":{"bld":130,"psn":89,"fst":93,"cur":101},"weight":26.5,"poise":25.35,"weight_class":"","desc":"Malformed black armor of the Ringed Knights. The armor of early men was forged in the Abyss, and betrays a smidgen of life.\nFor this reason the gods cast a seal of fire upon such armor, and those who possessed them.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Ringed Knights.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ringed_Knight_Set"},{"id":"ruin-set","kind":"armor","name":"Ruin Set","page":"Ruin Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Ruin_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":26.507,"strike":25.368,"slash":30.969,"thrust":26.507,"mag":24.871,"fire":22.625,"ltn":23.713,"dark":20.504},"res":{"bld":143,"psn":138,"fst":78,"cur":71},"weight":30.5,"poise":33.58,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the company of knights who were sent to the Ringed City on an old king's orders.\nThe knights sought the dark soul, but were so soundly crushed, they had little choice but to swear themselves to the Judicator Giant.\nThe ill-fated company was later immortalized in a dark fable, inspiring the aspect of certain golems in whom their name lived on.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>, on a corpse below the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Mausoleum Lookout<\/a> bonfire. After descending the stairs, take a hard right and walk under the stairs instead of towards the gravestones.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ruin_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sellsword-set","kind":"armor","name":"Sellsword Set","page":"Sellsword Set","img":"assets/img/Sellsword_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":20.056,"strike":21.008,"slash":19.564,"thrust":20.876,"mag":15.997,"fire":15.508,"ltn":12.582,"dark":15.43},"res":{"bld":129,"psn":83,"fst":81,"cur":55},"weight":18.7,"poise":17.75,"weight_class":"","desc":"Metal armor interwoven with coarse cloth. Able to endure the hardships of battle and prolonged travel.\nIt is light considering the build, striking a fine balance between absorption and substance.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Mercenary class.<\/li><li>Found within <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Crucifixion Woods<\/a>. On the far side of the swamp to the right, past two Lycanthropes, it is found on a corpse down a flight of stairs guarded by a Black Knight.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sellsword_Set"},{"id":"set-of-favor","kind":"armor","name":"Set of Favor","page":"Set of Favor (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Set_of_Favor__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":26.167,"strike":24.195,"slash":26.167,"thrust":26.746,"mag":22.355,"fire":23.279,"ltn":17.194,"dark":23.279},"res":{"bld":153,"psn":111,"fst":122,"cur":87},"weight":30,"poise":33.87,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the pitiable Embraced knight.\nDepicts the affection of the goddess Fina.\nThe face is crafted to depict the goddess's embrace, quite ignoring the fact that her love is in fact as fickle as the weather.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 31,000 souls after defeating the two Sulyvahn's Beasts in the Water Reserve.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Set_of_Favor_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"set-of-thorns","kind":"armor","name":"Set of Thorns","page":"Set of Thorns (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Set_of_Thorns__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":21.691,"strike":16.137,"slash":27.556,"thrust":22.621,"mag":14.529,"fire":14.529,"ltn":14.529,"dark":11.8},"res":{"bld":159,"psn":66,"fst":80,"cur":55},"weight":20.5,"poise":14.89,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of Kirk, the notorious knight of Thorns.\nA dense patch of thorns grows from its surface.\nA fitting item for the murderous Kirk, for even the simple act of rolling can damage enemies when wearing this attire.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>. After defeating Longfinger Kirk when he invades, go to <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Rosaria's Bed Chamber<\/a>, where it can be found on a corpse.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Set_of_Thorns_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"shadow-set","kind":"armor","name":"Shadow Set","page":"Shadow Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Shadow_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":14.339,"strike":12.062,"slash":10.21,"thrust":14.339,"mag":10.482,"fire":11.786,"ltn":14.51,"dark":9.66},"res":{"bld":68,"psn":97,"fst":95,"cur":86},"weight":8.8,"poise":5.69,"weight_class":"","desc":"Black cloth mask worn by spooks from an Eastern land. Sacrifices defense for greater mobility.\nThe late King Oceiros was obsessed by dragons, to the extent that he would later be known as the Consumed King. Countless assassins were sent to end his reign, but none returned.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>, on a corpse in the Toxic ground, under the terrace at the center of the garden.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Shadow_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"shiras-set","kind":"armor","name":"Shira's Set","page":"Shira's Set","img":"assets/img/Shira_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":13.775,"strike":16.58,"slash":13.775,"thrust":17.824,"mag":22.599,"fire":23.366,"ltn":22.356,"dark":17.883},"res":{"bld":75,"psn":133,"fst":126,"cur":147},"weight":13.6,"poise":6,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of Shira, knight in service to Filianore. A rare women's piece from ancient times.\nWith a spun gold shawl draped over the silver breastplate and a green woven skirt, this armor offers a subdued yet refined elegance, apropos to both a handmaiden of the Princess and one whose veins course with royal blood.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>. After defeating <a data-e=\"shira-knight-of-filianore\">Shira, Knight of Filianore<\/a> at <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Filianore's Rest<\/a>, return to her door within the Ringed City, at the top of the great stairway. Her door will now be open, and the set can be found on a corpse inside.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Shira's_Set"},{"id":"silver-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Silver Knight Set","page":"Silver Knight Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Silver_Knight_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":27.792,"strike":25.61,"slash":32.353,"thrust":31.192,"mag":26.006,"fire":25.285,"ltn":23.461,"dark":23.461},"res":{"bld":147,"psn":120,"fst":109,"cur":86},"weight":33.7,"poise":36.08,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the Silver Knights allegiant to the royals of old.\nIt is said that even after the family's passing, the knights continued to watch over their manor, and the ruined cathedral.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Silver Knights in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> and <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Silver_Knight_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"slave-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Slave Knight Set","page":"Slave Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Slave_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":26.501,"strike":21.771,"slash":26.501,"thrust":20.492,"mag":11.796,"fire":16.223,"ltn":11.796,"dark":14.524},"res":{"bld":145,"psn":80,"fst":84,"cur":48},"weight":20.9,"poise":18.34,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor issued to slave knights. The fine craftsmanship made this a symbol of honor.\nLong ago, only the Undead served as slave knights, warriors used as fodder in the bleakest of battles.\nThey grew decrepit, their skin charred black and their bones twisted. Eventually they went outright mad, but were never relieved from duty.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>. In the Corvian Settlement, navigate to the rooftops and into the tower with the ladder that leads to the bridge to the cliffside. Inside the tower is a drop-down which leads to a locked room with three <a data-e=\"forlorn-corvian-settler\">Forlorn Corvian Settlers<\/a> within. The set will be on a corpse inside.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Slave_Knight_Set"},{"id":"smoughs-set","kind":"armor","name":"Smough's Set","page":"Smough's Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Smough_s_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":35.807,"strike":36.47,"slash":34.989,"thrust":31.026,"mag":26.174,"fire":25.603,"ltn":27.067,"dark":26.312},"res":{"bld":159,"psn":159,"fst":159,"cur":143},"weight":60,"poise":49.43,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Grotesque armor associated with Smough, the last knight to stand in defense of the ruined cathedral.\nBoasts extremely high defense and can be donned by humans, but not without great difficulty.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 31,000 souls after defeating <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Smough's_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sorcerer-set","kind":"armor","name":"Sorcerer Set","page":"Sorcerer Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Sorcerer_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":9.857,"strike":10.51,"slash":9.857,"thrust":8.92,"mag":24.641,"fire":24.778,"ltn":25.265,"dark":25.281},"res":{"bld":66,"psn":97,"fst":88,"cur":152},"weight":10,"poise":3.66,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of a sorcerer from the Vinheim Dragon School. Long, ash-colored robes.\nUnderneath is a deep blue sorcerer's coat; conventional uniform of the academy.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Sorcerer class.<\/li><li>Found in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>. From the Crucifixion Woods bonfire, drop into the swamp and head towards the ruins. Before the stairs that lead into the ruins, there is a doorway that leads into a small room. The set can be found on a corpse inside, alongside the <a data-e=\"sage-ring\">Sage Ring<\/a>, guarded by a Lycanthrope.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sorcerer_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sunless-set","kind":"armor","name":"Sunless Set","page":"Sunless Set","img":"assets/img/Sunless_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":20.699,"strike":16.295,"slash":21.163,"thrust":20.377,"mag":22.844,"fire":20.218,"ltn":14.324,"dark":23.604},"res":{"bld":90,"psn":64,"fst":73,"cur":92},"weight":20.2,"poise":14.88,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of a knight from the Sunless Realms, known for their resistance to both magic and the dark.\nMetal plating and chainmail, treated with silver.\nSunless Knights serve the nameless moon, and perhaps it is for this reason the attire casts a feminine silhouette.","avail":"<p>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 23,000 souls once <a data-e=\"sirris-of-the-sunless-realms\">Sirris of the Sunless Realms<\/a> has died, whether she is killed by the player or upon completion of her questline.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sunless_Set"},{"id":"sunset-armor-set","kind":"armor","name":"Sunset Armor Set","page":"Sunset Set","img":"assets/img/Sunset_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":27.773,"strike":23.426,"slash":29.329,"thrust":27.317,"mag":18.869,"fire":22.135,"ltn":16.44,"dark":21.281},"res":{"bld":153,"psn":140,"fst":95,"cur":100},"weight":29.5,"poise":27.06,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of Hodrick, holy knight of Sunless Realms.\nThis light gold armor, named for its sunset hues, is now faded and wrapped in tainted rags.\nThe sorry fool was known to wander the battlefield as a crazed ghoul, lashing out at friend and foe alike.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Pit of Hollows<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, after defeating <a data-e=\"holy-knight-hodrick\">Holy Knight Hodrick<\/a> alongside <a data-e=\"sirris-of-the-sunless-realms\">Sirris of the Sunless Realms<\/a> during her questline.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sunset_Set"},{"id":"undead-legion-set","kind":"armor","name":"Undead Legion Set","page":"Undead Legion Set","img":"assets/img/Undead_Legion_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":20.503,"strike":20.668,"slash":12.254,"thrust":18.072,"mag":24.704,"fire":25.365,"ltn":25.695,"dark":20.834},"res":{"bld":101,"psn":130,"fst":161,"cur":109},"weight":18.6,"poise":10.23,"weight_class":"","desc":"Attire of the Abyss Watchers, the Undead Legion of Farron.\nThese undead warriors vowed to partake of wolf blood.\nThey acted in the dark, seeking out any sign of the Abyss, fighting a constant war with its abominations.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 31,000 souls after defeating the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Undead_Legion_Set"},{"id":"vilhelms-set","kind":"armor","name":"Vilhelm's Set","page":"Vilhelm's Set","img":"assets/img/Vilhelm_s_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":25.518,"strike":20.492,"slash":25.518,"thrust":28.511,"mag":19.2,"fire":24.612,"ltn":11.796,"dark":22.699},"res":{"bld":105,"psn":84,"fst":88,"cur":73},"weight":26.1,"poise":25.7,"weight_class":"","desc":"The black armor of Vilhelm, Knight of Londor, and a nice fit for any lean Hollow.\nThis hollow knight, who served the three sisters who founded the Sable Church, was particularly loyal to the eldest, and was known as a cold-blooded hangman.","avail":"<p>Found within the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>. Within the rotting basement of <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Ariandel Chapel<\/a>, several Giant Flies guard it and other loot on the lower level.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Vilhelm's_Set"},{"id":"winged-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Winged Knight Set","page":"Winged Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Winged_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":34.123,"strike":28.491,"slash":34.123,"thrust":32.626,"mag":26.554,"fire":27.137,"ltn":27.996,"dark":31.284},"res":{"bld":168,"psn":142,"fst":157,"cur":100},"weight":41.7,"poise":43.24,"weight_class":"Heavy","desc":"Armor of the Winged Knights, named for their appearance, who swore themselves to the Angels.\nWorship of the divine messengers was viewed as heresy in Lothric and unrecognized by any of the Three Pillars of rule.\nThird paragraph - This is believed to be why Gertrude, the Heavenly Daughter, was imprisoned in the lofty cell of the Grand Archives.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>. From the initial bonfire, traverse up the pathway and enter the room with the ladder and the <a data-e=\"winged-knight-twinaxess\">axe<\/a>-wielding Winged Knight. At the top of the stairs, hit the rightmost panel of the backt wall to reveal an Illusory Wall. The set can be found on a corpse in front of a painting of a Winged Knight.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Winged_Knight_Set"},{"id":"wolf-knight-set","kind":"armor","name":"Wolf Knight Set","page":"Wolf Knight Set","img":"assets/img/Wolf_Knight_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":23.766,"strike":20.561,"slash":23.845,"thrust":23.845,"mag":16.036,"fire":22.843,"ltn":11.424,"dark":20.475},"res":{"bld":112,"psn":76,"fst":83,"cur":83},"weight":21.4,"poise":16.14,"weight_class":"","desc":"Armor of a knight tainted by the dark of the Abyss. The twilight blue cape is damp, and will ever remain so.\nA vanquished knight left behind only wolf's blood, and his legacy of duty. The Undead Legion of Farron was formed to bear his torch, and the armor of these Abyss Watchers suggests their own eventual end.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Dark Firelink Shrine<\/a> for a total of 46,000 souls after defeating the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Wolf_Knight_Set"},{"id":"worker-set","kind":"armor","name":"Worker Set","page":"Worker Set","img":"assets/img/Worker_Set.webp","defs":{"phys":9.756,"strike":14.428,"slash":11.795,"thrust":11.795,"mag":14.517,"fire":11.791,"ltn":11.791,"dark":22.686},"res":{"bld":84,"psn":165,"fst":105,"cur":145},"weight":10.8,"poise":5.68,"weight_class":"","desc":"Garb worn by inhabitants of the Undead Settlement.\nOfficial attire for the dissection and burial of undead. Naturally the ceremonial significance of such work is long forgotten.\nIndeed, no one could continue to entertain such horrors.","avail":"<p>Drop from the Peasant Hollows in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Worker_Set"},{"id":"xanthous-set","kind":"armor","name":"Xanthous Set","page":"Xanthous Set (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Xanthous_Set__Dark_Souls_III.webp","defs":{"phys":17.548,"strike":15.666,"slash":16.987,"thrust":16.906,"mag":23.774,"fire":11.793,"ltn":22.961,"dark":23.449},"res":{"bld":97,"psn":130,"fst":114,"cur":95},"weight":17.5,"poise":10.98,"weight_class":"","desc":"Yellowish overcoat covering a band of brass medallions.\nXanthous clothing is the mark of a researcher of lost sorceries, and the number of medallions denotes their success. A point of prided for the researchers, even if its signficance is lost on others.","avail":"<ul><li>The set, minus the crown, is sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for a total of 24,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"xanthous-ashes\">Xanthous Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>The Xanthous Crown can be obtained twice within the same playthrough:<ol><li>Dropped by Yellowfinger Heysel after defeating her at either Crucifixion Woods or <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. She will only drop it once.<\/li><li>Dropped by the Man-grub that spawns in <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Rosaria's Bed Chamber<\/a> after the first three Lords of Cinder (excluding Ludleth) have been killed.<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Xanthous_Set_(Dark_Souls_III)"}]);
